{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Moses will speak and Elohim will answer him in a voice.</b> It was a great wonder that all Israel, who were spread over three parasangs, should all hear the voice of Moses — and moreover the sound of the shofar was there and should have drowned it out. Therefore Scripture explains the great miracle wrought in this: that Moses will speak and Elohim grants him strength and aid in his voice, so that he can raise it to the measure that all Israel hear his voice and understand it. And the word יעננו is in the sense of (Hosea 2:23) ״אענה נאם ה׳ אענה את השמים״ — 'I will answer, says YHWH; I will answer the heavens' — which is the language of help and aid."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:08.820468294Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}